course: dictionary
lesson: 8656
title: The seaside
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Seaside is a word you can use as a noun or an adjective. As a noun, it names a place: the seaside is a place by the sea, especially a beach or town where people go on holiday. «At the seaside a gull snatches a chip out of Chloe's hand.» Here seaside is the place where it happens.
explain: As an adjective, seaside describes something as being by the sea. «We stayed in a seaside town.» The word seaside tells you which kind of town it is. Try swapping in a different word, such as «a town by the sea», and see if the meaning still fits.
explain: Look at the words around seaside to check its meaning. Holidays, sandcastles, piers, ice cream and rock pools all tell you the context is the sea and the beach. When you meet seaside in a history or science text, the clues around it will help you understand it.
fact: The seaside is a place by the sea, especially a beach or town where people go on holiday.
fact: As an adjective, seaside means by the sea, as in «a seaside town».
fact: Seaside can be a noun, as in «at the seaside», or an adjective, as in «a seaside promenade».
fact: «On a sunny day at the seaside the land warms faster than the sea, so a cool sea breeze blows onto the beach.»
fact: Safety at the seaside: swim between the flags, watch the tide, wear sun cream, and stay near adults.
exercise: What does seaside mean in «at the seaside a gull snatches a chip»? | A place in a city with no water | A deep cave under the hills | A school for learning to swim | *A place by the sea, often a beach or town people visit on holiday
exercise: «We stayed in a seaside town.» What does seaside tell us about the town? | *It is by the sea | It has no shops | It is on top of a mountain | It is under the ground
exercise: Find and copy the word for the bird that snatches chips from a child's hand in «Anyone who has eaten chips on a seaside promenade knows the gull». | promenade | *gull | chips | child's
test: «On a sunny day at the seaside, a cool sea breeze blows onto the beach.» Where does the sea breeze blow? | Into the mountains | *Onto the beach | Into the school hall | Under the road
test: Which is the safest thing to do at the seaside? | Wander off alone to explore the rocks | *Stay near an adult and swim between the flags | Swim far away from the flags | Go in the water when the tide is coming in without telling anyone
exam: In «We built sandcastles at the seaside», what kind of word is seaside? | Adverb | Adjective | *Noun | Verb
